# Per-operator secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Per-operator Obsidian state (workspace layout, hot-reload cache).
# Keep app.json / community-plugins.json / core-plugins.json / appearance.json
# checked in so a fresh clone inherits the vault's plugin set.
.obsidian/workspace*.json
.obsidian/cache/
.obsidian/hotkeys.json

# obsidian-local-rest-api stores apiKey + RSA private key + TLS cert in
# its data.json on first enable. NEVER commit — the plugin regenerates
# these on first enable per-operator, so each clone gets its own keys.
# (Other plugin data.json files stay tracked so fresh clones inherit
# usable defaults; they're audited free of credentials.)
.obsidian/plugins/obsidian-local-rest-api/data.json

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Tooling caches
node_modules/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# graphify's output, ALL of it — the semantic embedding cache (7,332 of the
# 7,344 files, ~80MB, churning ~800 files per refresh) and, since HIMMEL-1960,
# the top-level products too (graph.json, GRAPH_REPORT.md, the per-corpus
# graphs, manifest.json).
#
# WHY the products stopped being tracked (operator decision (b), 2026-08-19):
# the graphmap cadence runs `graphify update` against this vault IN PLACE, and
# this vault has an auto-committer. Tracked products therefore meant a commit
# of graph churn on every structural refresh — noise in a personal vault's
# history, generated wholly from content the same history already carries.
#
# COST, stated plainly: these products are what `graphify query`/`explain` and
# the 60-Maps/graphify-*-map.md notes read. A fresh clone on ANOTHER MACHINE
# now has no graph at all until it runs a refresh there, where before it
# inherited the last committed one (stale, but present). The graph became a
# per-machine local artifact rather than a synced one. Regenerate with
# `graphify update <vault> --force`, or the himmel cadence's structural leg.
graphify-out/

# Claude worktrees
/.claude/worktrees/
/.worktrees/
/.claude/settings.local.json

# Per-machine hook logs. These append-only logs are written by the
# end-session-wiki hook on every machine that opens the vault; committing
# them to a shared repo produced a merge conflict on every cross-machine
# pull. Config (end-session-wiki.json) stays tracked; only the logs are local.
**/.claude/*.log

# Single-writer opt-in marker. A per-clone, gitignored file that designates
# THIS clone as committing/pushing straight to main by design (a personal,
# local-only vault). setup.{sh,ps1} create it for a local vault with no remote;
# the guardrail predicates (scripts/guardrails/lib.sh) honor it. A clone WITHOUT
# the marker stays protected by worktree-isolation, so it never travels via git.
.single-writer

# Handover scratch state
.last-consolidate.json
.pending-new-item.json

# Vault-template upgrade state (HIMMEL-389). The version stamp (.vault-template.json)
# IS tracked — it travels with the vault. These are upgrade-managed scratch:
# the 3-way-merge base snapshot, an unresolved _CLAUDE.md conflict sidecar, and
# any temp left by an interrupted atomic write.
.vault-template.base/
*.template-merge
*.upgrade-tmp.*

# Obsidian graph cache + per-chat asset dumps (machine-local)
.obsidian/graph.json
chats/*/_assets/

# Judge/leg scratch dirs (probe scripts, extracted repo trees) — never vault content.
handovers/**/verdicts/*/scratch/
